WEBVTT

00:05:58.916 --> 00:06:02.436
Again, it takes a certain person
of a certain disposition to do this stuff,

00:06:02.476 --> 00:06:05.596
but you can’t feel it on the inside,
it’s fine, it’s cold outside.

00:06:05.596 --> 00:06:06.756
And we’re moving around,

00:06:06.756 --> 00:06:09.596
and if you look out the window,
we're looking mostly at mud.

00:06:09.596 --> 00:06:12.796
Imagine all that stuff
that has come down from the surface.

00:06:12.836 --> 00:06:14.316
All that lovely organic matter.

00:06:14.356 --> 00:06:16.796
It's carbon, it's taking carbon
from the atmosphere,

00:06:16.796 --> 00:06:18.476
it's being absorbed into the ocean.

00:06:18.516 --> 00:06:21.636
The surface of oceans basically comes
down and sinks into the mud.

00:06:21.636 --> 00:06:23.356
What happens to the carbon?

00:06:23.356 --> 00:06:26.556
The bottom of the trenches,
the reason why the trenches are so deep,

00:06:26.596 --> 00:06:28.996
the reason why they're
11 kilometers in some places

00:06:28.996 --> 00:06:32.036
is because two tectonic plates
hit each other.